  "core_message": "The Solway Firth “spaceman” was simply Jim Templeton’s wife walking into the frame, not an extraterrestrial.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "Blue Dress Mistaken for Spaceman in 1964 Marsh Photo",
  "description": "In 1964 a photograph taken at Burgh Marsh seemed to show a figure in a space suit. Decades of speculation followed until investigators revealed the simple truth – it was the photographer’s wife, Annie, caught in the background. This short explains how a camera’s viewfinder limitation created a modern UFO legend.\n\nThe story highlights how everyday details can turn into mysterious myths.\n\nSources: Wikipedia page on Solway Firth Spaceman; BBC interview with David Clarke; Daily Mail letter 2002.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Solway Firth Spaceman\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solway_Firth_Spaceman), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.",
